# .gitignore for the team KB.

# Obsidian: per-person state. Opening a note rewrites these (runs/07-obsidian-config.txt).
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspaces.json
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/appearance.json
.obsidian/themes/
# Core plugin on/off switches: personal, and Obsidian's defaults already turn Templates on.
.obsidian/core-plugins.json
# Plugins: code and per-person plugin state. Plugin data files can hold note text and conflict
# (Zeppla, 27 Aug merge). The team plugin list lives in the onboarding note instead.
.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/community-plugins.json
# Optional, if the team adopts a plugin: commit its SETTINGS but never its code (tested with
# git ls-files). Only for plugins whose data.json holds settings, not per-person state, note text
# or keys. To use: replace the two lines above with these four, uncommented, plugin id filled in.
# .obsidian/plugins/*
# !.obsidian/plugins/<plugin-id>/
# .obsidian/plugins/<plugin-id>/*
# !.obsidian/plugins/<plugin-id>/data.json
# Committed on purpose: .obsidian/app.json (wikilinks, shortest names, update links on rename)
# so a new clone starts with the team's link settings; kb-doctor checks it did not change.
.trash/
conflict-files-obsidian-git.md

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Agents: personal settings only. Shared ones (.claude/settings.json, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md,
# .claude/skills/, .agents/skills/) are committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.override.md
